Cure sickness might make the difference when fighting against Pestilence.
As for attack spells, magic missile and FoD are enough. Extra healing
is also nice, but not necessary if you have saved lots of blessed !oFH.

Fireball is almost useless, and the only use I can think for cone of cold
is freezing water in the Plane of Water. I'm not sure if it's possible!

If you practice healing to skilled, you should be able to use a small
shield, adding more AC points.
A few more XP levels woudn't hurt... but that's only my opinion.

You could try a radical trick when fighting by spellcasting:
drop the Amulet of Yendor and shoot the enemies with FoD and MM.
Now it won't drain your power. The downsides are that you must
pick up the amulet, and it just might get mixed with cheap plastic
imitations. Not a great trick on Water, Air or Fire or when you're generally
levitating. Also, you'll have to stand still on the Amulet so nobody will
steal it.

If you get in a wrong temple, stay there and let your power get back up.
Of course, a Rider might follow you there quickly.

When and if your pet angel dies (not before!), you could try using
conflict. Maybe, just maybe, the Riders will suffer enough from this.

